frontend (AdrenoMetal NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm as the k27 tree's scripts/piano-frontend-patch.py leaves it): the console after a login

- NBLOG's stderr copy (NMB_LOG_STDERR, which the kernel's stderr-log=1 puts on the console) is rate-limited per call site: the first
  8 lines, then the 16th, 32nd, 64th, ... with the count ("[#64] ..."). The unified log and the problem notes still get every line.
- "native-metal: no device answer: ..." (harmlessProblem; five or six per Metal process) goes to the unified log only.
- computeCommandEncoderWithDispatchType: with MTLDispatchTypeConcurrent returns the serial encoder (as computeCommandEncoderWithDescriptor:
  already did for a concurrent pass) instead of refusing the command buffer; one line per process says so.
Applied by tooling/metal/build-turnip-a830.sh to out/turnip-a830/plugin/frontend.mm. MIT, as the file.

